description =
    A watch and an app designed to help people with dementia and their families live more worry-free lives.
content =
    WatchOut combines familiar design with modern technology to provide safety for people with
    dementia and the support their families need in everyday life.
    <br>
    Dementia doesn’t just change the lives of those affected, but also of those who care for them.
    WatchOut helps relatives keep a clear overview of the situation and respond quickly when needed
    – without overwhelming the person affected with complex technology.
    <br>
    WatchOut consists of two components: a digital "analogue" watch and an easy-to-use companion app.
    Together, they provide security, orientation, and an intuitive experience.

watch = Watch
watch-idea =
    As people with dementia often retain familiar daily routines, the watch has been deliberately
    designed with a classic analogue look.
    At first glance, it appears as a traditional wristwatch – something recognisable and
    reliable in everyday life.
watch-features =
    The watch features a clearly readable dial with large numbers and bold hands.
    Its soft, ergonomically rounded case helps prevent injury.
    Despite its familiar appearance, it is equipped with smart technology:
    It transmits GPS data, automatically detects falls, and includes an emergency call
    function via two discreet buttons.
    The time can be set manually using a traditional crown,
    making the watch a familiar and easy-to-use companion for the wearer.

app = Companion App
app-general =
    The app is designed to give family members a quick and easy overview without unnecessary complexity.
    The home screen displays all recent events at a glance, clearly arranged by time and colour-coded
    according to urgency.
    This allows changes in the daily routine of the person affected to be recognised immediately.
app-call-history =
    The app also makes it possible to contact the watch wearer, saved contacts or an emergency
    service directly.
    A separate section displays past events such as location history or recorded emergencies,
    allowing developments to be tracked and understood over time.
app-map =
    An integrated map shows the current location of the person with dementia as well as the
    positions of connected family members and trusted friends.
    This helps with coordination in everyday life and provides everyone involved with greater
    peace of mind.
